1. FROM : used for utuilizing a base image (pulled from docker hub) also specification of OS or programming language, over which additional layers of docker images are built.

2. RUN : used to build new layer over base image.

opitions: 

i) --device

ii) --mount (analogy of a pendrive), gives the container extra things to access.

RUN --mount=type=cache  : prev. build stored as cache, speeds up future build of same thing.

RUN --mount=type=secret  : api key not stored in built image, only used during build and then removed.

RUN --mount=type=ssh    : ssh key used only in build stage and removed after it. (to clone pvt repo).

--network 

--security


3.*CMD: tells the cmd which has to be run by the container.

CMD ["executable", "param1"]  <--format

executable : which tool or sw to be used. (permanent)

param1: over which it has to be used. (can be overridden)

eg: CMD ["python", "app.py"]  --> python runs app.py

docker run image hello.py ---> python now instead runs hello.py


4.*LABEL: metadata about the image (in key:value pairs)

decription, version, ""=""

multilabel:  LABEL multi.label1="value1" multi.label2="value2" 

overriding is done here too.

Inspect label:  docker image inspect --format='{{json .Config.Labels}}' myimage


5.*COPY: copies file,dir from source(porject) to the dest.(docker image).

Format: COPY src dest

. : current directory in build context

.. : current directory in image

COPY ..   ==    COPY . /app  ==   WORKDIR /app


6.*ENV: sets envvironment variable in ky value pairs.

format: ENV MY_NAME:"SANTY" MY_DEPT:"CYS"

Persistence: environmental variable set using ENV will persisit if container run from resulting image.

eg:
```
FROM ubuntu

ENV NAME=santhosh
```

```
now build:  docker build -t myimage .
```

```
docker run myimage    
````

```
op: santhosh
```

Overriding :   docker run --env {key}:{value}

**docker --> image --> container built from the image (has env variable).


Inheritance: environmental variables inherited from a earlier stage or parent base image.

stage 1
```
FROM ubuntu as base
```

```
ENV APP=myAPP
```

```
FROM base
```

```
RUN echo $APP
```

stage 2:

```
FROM base
```

```
APP=myAPP
```



